# Solemnity's ruling: "If ... an additional cost of a spell requires putting counters on an artifact, creature, enchantment, or land,
# that cost can't be paid" (CR 118.3, 101.2). Requiting Hex's "you may blight 1" puts a -1/-1 counter on a creature its caster
# controls (CR 701.68a); with Solemnity out Bot1's Ornithopter can't take one, so the attempted blight cast rolls back and the Hex is
# cast plain: the Elves dies and no life is gained. The positive control is
# requiting-hex-blighting-your-own-creature-puts-the-counter-on-it-and-gains-two-life, the same choice taken with an Ornithopter.

